>leonard@mimsy.umd.edu (Leonard Dickens) writes:
>
>What alignment do you favor?

I've found chaotic to be the best.

>It seems to me that the best alignment
>to be is Lawful, for the following reasons:
>1) Two of the best artifacts (Mjollnir, Excaliber) available from god.

 Really? I always thought Excaliber was highly overrated. In any case,
if one really wants it, Excaliber can also be obtained somewhat more
easily from a fountain.

>2) Can convert any altar to Lawful, which is good because:
>3) Lawful altars make holy water, i.e., blessings.
>
>Any dissention on this point?

   This is convenient, true, but I've never found it to be critical.
Finding holy water has never been a real big problem for me. I
usually find a lawful alter somewhere in the game. If I find one
early I make sure to convert some water to holy water before I
change the alter's alignment - one bottle of holy water is all you
need. If I don't find a lawful alter early there are other ways
to get holy water.

>Chaotic characters *do* have a good
>chance of getting Stormbringer from their god.

  This is what tips the balance for me. There are simply too many
lawful artifacts. Getting Mjollnir can take forever. (Although I
have had games where the gods give me Grimtooth and Cleaver and then
become stingy for a *long* while before finally bestowing
Stormbringer.

  Another reason I prefer chaotic alignment is that I would just
as soon avoid fighting homunculi and gremlins, both chaotic. On the
other hand I like to fight lawful dwarves since they often have nice
armor like iron shoes, hard hats, dwarvish shields and mithrilcotes
and are a nice source of pick-axes.

